/-!
# The twisted inverse image of a Koszul-regular closed immersion: the top degree

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of schemes, `X` quasi-compact and quasi-separated, whose
defining ideal sheaf `J` is, near every point of `Z`, generated by a Koszul-regular sequence of
`r` sections, and let `c` be the right adjoint of `Ri_*` on `D_QCoh`. Then

`c(𝒪_X) ≅ ⋀ʳ 𝒩[-r]`,

where `𝒩` is the normal sheaf of `i`.

By `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.KoszulRegularRightAdjoint.Vanishing`, `c(𝒪_X)` is its
degree-`r` cohomology sheaf `H` placed in degree `r`, and `i_*H = 𝓔xtʳ(𝒪_X/J, 𝒪_X)` is the
degree-`r` piece of the self-Ext algebra `𝓔xt^•(𝒪_X/J, 𝒪_X/J)`. That algebra is the exterior
algebra of its degree-one piece ([Stacks, Tag 0BQY]), which is `i_*𝒩` by [Stacks, Tag 0BQW].
Descending the algebra along `𝒪_X/J ≅ i_*𝒪_Z` and comparing exterior powers across the
pushforward along `i` gives `i_*H ≅ i_*⋀ʳ𝒩`, and `i_*` is fully faithful.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.KoszulRegular.pushforwardExteriorPowerIso`: the pushforward of `⋀ⁿ N` is the
  degree-`n` piece of the self-Ext algebra whenever the degree-one piece is `i_*N`.
* `Stacks.Duality.KoszulRegular.pushforwardNormalSheafIsoSelfExtOne`: `i_*𝒩 ≅ 𝓔xt¹(𝒪_X/J, 𝒪_X/J)`.
* `Stacks.Duality.KoszulRegular.twistedInverseImageIso`: `⋀ʳ 𝒩[-r] ≅ c(𝒪_X)`.
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction
open HomologicalComplex TopologicalSpace CategoryTheory.Sheaf
